# Copy to .env in the workspace root. That filename is gitignored; this example
# is deliberately not, so the variable NAMES can be published without values.
#
# None of this is needed to install, to evaluate a provided checkpoint, or to
# run the learning recipe. Evaluation and training use a local checkpoint and a
# local engine and contact no network service. These variables exist only for
# the optional language-model agent path (`factoriorl doctor-agent`,
# `factoriorl preflight --live`, `factoriorl agent`, `factoriorl demo`), which
# does call a paid API if you point it at one. Every one of those goes through
# a spend cap: there is no code path that dispatches an unbudgeted request.
#
# How the value is used: the file seeds the process environment, and a
# credential is then read from the environment and nowhere else. No adapter
# takes a file path. An already-exported variable wins over this file, so an
# explicit export is never silently overridden. Adapters hold the key privately
# and redact it from everything written to a run directory -- an endpoint that
# echoes an Authorization header into a 401 body would otherwise land verbatim
# in decisions.jsonl, and run directories get shared as evidence.
#
# Set only the one your endpoint needs. A local inference server usually needs
# none at all: pass --api-key-env '' and leave every line below commented.

# Used by tools/demonstration.py and the watch/build/recovery agent tools.
#OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Used by AnthropicMessagesAdapter, reachable from the CLI with
# `--adapter anthropic` on `doctor-agent` and `preflight`.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The roadmap's A5 attempt runs against DeepSeek. Named here because the
# repository was documenting every provider except the one its own paid run
# uses, which made the paid path undiscoverable from a fresh checkout:
#
#   factoriorl preflight --live        # one capped call, a fraction of a cent
#   factoriorl agent --task open_factory --clock realtime --launch-client
#       --model deepseek-flash --base-url https://api.deepseek.com/v1
#       --api-key-env DEEPSEEK_API_KEY --max-cost-usd 2
#DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Any OpenAI-compatible gateway works through OpenAICompatibleAdapter; the
# base URL is configuration, not a constant. Point --base-url at it and name
# whichever variable holds its key.
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Not a credential: a default model name for the agent tools.
#FRRL_AGENT_MODEL=

# Not a credential either, and not read from this file -- engine settings live
# in .factoriorl.user.json or the FACTORIO_RL_ENGINE variable. Listed here only
# because people look for them in .env first.
#FACTORIO_RL_ENGINE=
#FACTORIO_RL_GAME_SPEED=
